.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Days after learning of Volta&#x27;s newly announced pile, William Nicholson and Anthony Carlisle connected one to a bowl of water in May 1800 and watched gas bubble from each wire -- the first electrolysis, and the first new discovery the pile made possible. This example reconstructs both halves of that observation from functions already in this package: the theoretical minimum decomposition voltage of water (~chemistrykit.electrochem.systems.electrolysis.minimum_applied_voltage_electrolytic, applied to the tabulated H+/H2 and O2/H2O standard potentials) comes out at the textbook 1.23 V, and Faraday&#x27;s law (~chemistrykit.electrochem.systems.electrolysis.moles_from_charge) recovers the 2:1 hydrogen-to-oxygen ratio Nicholson and Carlisle actually saw bubbling from the two wires, directly from electron-transfer stoichiometry.">

